    "image_with_collapsible_content_D8wEce": {
      "type": "image-with-collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_gQH9Dg": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Superior Absorption",
            "row_content": "<ul><li>Many vitamins and minerals must undergo enzymatic conversion in the body to become \"bioactive\"—the form your cells can actually use. However, this conversion process can be inefficient or impaired in individuals with certain genetic variations or metabolic conditions.<br/></li><li>We use <em>pre-activated nutrient forms</em>, which bypass this conversion step. This improves <strong>bioavailability</strong>—the proportion of a nutrient that enters circulation and can be used by the body—ensuring more of the supplement works for you and less is wasted.<br/><br/></li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_M6nycn": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Improved effectiveness",
            "row_content": "<ul><li>The more absorbable a supplement is, the more of its active ingredients reach your bloodstream and tissues. In contrast, lower-quality formulations may pass through your digestive system largely unabsorbed, reducing their intended effects.</li><li>High-absorption supplements are more likely to support optimal nutrient status and health outcomes.<br/><br/></li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_nkqQGY": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Quicker results",
            "row_content": "<ul><li>When nutrients are absorbed more efficiently, they begin acting in the body more quickly. </li><li>This can translate to <strong>faster symptom help </strong>or <strong>quicker support</strong> for functions like <strong>energy, mood, or hormonal balance.<br/></strong><br/></li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_zRHQbQ": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Reduced side effects",
            "row_content": "<ul><li>Poorly absorbed supplements can place extra strain on your digestive system, <strong>sometimes leading to bloating, nausea, or discomfort. </strong></li><li>Highly absorbable forms <strong>reduce the need for extensive digestive processing,</strong> making them gentler and more suitable for sensitive individuals.<br/><br/></li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
